  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that switching the RNA encoder from PCA (config_025, 0.6352) to scVI (config_037, 0.7062) yielded a ~7-point accuracy gain, confirming that a learned RNA representation is the most impactful design axis. However, we have only tested one learned encoder (scVI). Config_049 (scGPT, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) isolates the question of whether the specific learned encoder matters or whether any learned representation suffices, while holding all other settings at their proven-best values. If scGPT matches scVI, we learn the key insight is 'use a learned encoder' and can redirect budget to other axes (e.g., aggregation). If scGPT underperforms, we confirm scVI's architecture is specifically important. This reduces uncertainty on the highest-leverage untested design dimension, making it the most informative use of the next experiment."
}

